# LUMBRA — Major Art Style Update: "Fog Silhouette"

You are working on **LUMBRA**, a single-file rhythm runner (`index.html`, ~2,260 lines, no build step, no dependencies). Rework the game's **visual style** to match the attached reference image: a layered, misty, monochrome silhouette world (in the style of *Limbo* / *Geometry Dash* silhouette levels) in which only the interactive hazards carry color.

This is an **art-only** update. The gameplay, timing, physics, level charts, music and hitboxes must stay exactly the same.

---

## 0. Hard rules (read first)

1. **Do NOT touch the interactive hazards.** Leave all drawing code, colors, glows, animations and sizes for these exactly as they are:
   - Every entry in `HAZ` (`Bloom`, `Halo`, `Drift`, `Fade`, `Prism`, `Anchor`, `Rail`, `Rift`, `Comet`, `Thermal`, `Mimic`, `Glass`, `Coil`, `Flicker`, `Zenith`) and their `col` values.
   - In `RENDER.frame`: the **zone fields** block (`for (const z of L.zones)`), the **hazard tiles / coils / rails** block (`q.kind` = `F`, `X`, `1`, `2`, and so on, plus `L.coils` and `L.rails`), and every `case` in the obstacles `switch` **except `case "L"`**: `bl`, `ha`, `ke`, `ga`, `ri`, `co`, `ey`, `em`.
   - `glow()`, `glowSprite()`, the `COL` map, and the Zenith colored edge line on flipped terrain (`g.fillStyle = COL.Z; …`).
   - These elements must still be the **only saturated color** in the playfield and must stay drawn **on top of** the new fog layers so they read clearly.
2. **Do not change `SIM`, `LEVELS`, `HOME`, `FIXES`, `DEMO_SOL`, `MUSIC`, or game logic.** Never change any collision box, `o.x0/x1/y0/y1`, segment top, or timing value. Every visual must line up with the existing collision geometry: spike tips at the same height, ground top edges at exactly `Y(q.top)`.
3. Keep everything in the single `index.html`. Add no external assets, images, fonts or libraries. Everything is procedural canvas drawing, as it is now.
4. Performance: the game must hold 60 fps on mid-range phones. Pre-render static layers to offscreen canvases (as `BACKDROPS.strip` already does). Don't add per-frame `shadowBlur` or `filter` on the main canvas. Respect the existing `quality` / `lowQ` fallback (`RENDER.setQuality(0.72)`).
5. Keep `prefers-reduced-motion` behavior: no new camera sway or parallax bob beyond what already exists when reduced motion is on.

